The Power of Search Engines: Beyond the First Result
Most users rely on search engines, but few know how to use them effectively. 
Learning advanced search techniques, such as using quotation marks for exact phrases,
minus signs to exclude terms, and site-specific searches, can dramatically improve results.
It is also important to understand that search results are not always neutral; they can be influenced by algorithms, personalization, and even advertising.
Cross-referencing information across multiple sources and evaluating the credibility of websites are essential habits for anyone who uses the internet to learn or make decisions.
